WEBVTT

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:23.770
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:31.110
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:38.850
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:44.990
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:49.700
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:57.470
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:04.450
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:12.380
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:20.050
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:32.740
Can I have some more?

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:33.730
Yes, dear.

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:37.000
Nice to have some home
cooking, eh, son?

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:40.410
Yeah, it's a nice change
for a bachelor like me.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.940
You've got to hurry up and
find yourself a wife, Ken.

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:45.480
Here you are!

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:47.750
How are things going between
you and Miyuki?

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.290
Us? Umm... well... uh...

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:55.760
At this rate, you'll never
get things going.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.800
You certainly don't
take after me!

00:01:57.970 --> 00:01:59.800
What do you want me to do about it?!

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:03.130
Gee. I just want grandchildren, that's all.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.540
Grandchildren?!

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:08.200
Yeah! I think I can get along with her!

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:10.780
I think we'd be great as mother-in-law
and daughter-in-law!

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.240
Daughter-in-law? Mother-
in-law? What?

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:20.280
FILE. 29
A RIVAL APPEARS:
A HEATED RACE

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:36.430
Young people should
be falling in love...

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:40.270
...on a beautiful
day like this.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.740
Natsumi! Sit up and smarten up!
You're on duty, you know!

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:48.370
A young woman's springtime
is short and fleeting...

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.010
...as we can plainly
see today. Hmm?

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.060
Is anything wrong?

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.960
Is anything wrong?
Yeah... I've busted the clutch.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:01.130
So he says...

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:02.220
Then I'm up.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:04.700
Look! B-Motors.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.060
This bike seems to be custom-built.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.440
This is just temporary, so you should get
the clutch cable changed soon, okay?

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:16.940
I will. Thanks. That's
a big help.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.910
<i>Hmm... Not bad.</i>

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:20.850
Natsumi!

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:22.180
Umm! Umm! Umm! Umm!

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:25.720
You certainly are
a talented cop.

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:27.720
Even better than some of the
professional mechanics.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.920
No, not at all. This is just
a hobby of mine.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:34.790
There you go... All done.
Go easy on it, okay?

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:35.700
Sure will.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:36.530
Well then...

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:37.300
Umm...

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.260
Yes?

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.330
I was wondering if...

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:43.460
...you've heard of a shop around
here called "Zapper?"

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:44.840
It's my relative's place.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.330
Zapper?

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:49.000
That's Daimaru's shop!
You mean that...

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.840
You're related to Daimaru?
You're related to Daimaru?

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:53.000
Uh... Yes, I am.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.870
You're Sena's cousin?

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:59.850
I thought he was too nice a guy
to be related to Daimaru.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:03.220
We've become good
friends with Sena.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:07.550
I'm Yuichi Okazaki. Sena told
me she'd gotten married...

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.630
...so I came to see them
as soon as I could.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:13.060
Yuichi's so busy with his racing, he
couldn't come to our wedding.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.470
Sorry about that.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:15.400
His racing?

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.370
Aha! Now I remember!
His racing?

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:18.670
Look, Miyuki! Over there!

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:19.230
What?

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:22.500
It's him! Yuichi Okazaki, number 5
in the 250cc National Grand Prix!

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.970
Guilty as charged.

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:28.600
Hard to believe a pro racer would break
his clutch cable in the middle of town.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:30.110
Sena!

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.220
Can I have your autograph?!
Pretty please?

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:33.580
Natsumi!

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:36.750
Everyone at our station
is a big fan!

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.780
Is that right? You
flatter me.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.990
At first glance, your driving
looks rough and wobbly...

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.660
...but when the pressure is on,
your talent shines through.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:49.490
Miyuki, you sure he doesn't remind
you of someone else?

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:51.640
What do you mean?!

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:53.710
Must have a cold.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:55.070
Move it! Move it!

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:55.580
Get out of my way!

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:57.640
Hey! Wait!

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:59.800
Stop right there,
Scooter Mama!

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:00.950
Hey! My license!

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:10.080
Speaking of which... You and Ken
kind of have similar riding styles.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:11.290
Right, Miyuki?

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.890
What are you asking me for?

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:15.360
It's certainly nothing to blush about.

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:17.360
Who's Ken?

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:18.470
My son.

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:19.160
Son?!

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:22.670
Yeah. I keep telling him to
give me grandchildren...

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:25.290
...but he can't seem to
get things going.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:26.670
Grandchildren?

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:29.600
Although, it seems
he has a girlfriend.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:34.710
Is that right? He has
a girlfriend, huh?

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:40.740
Look at the time! We'd better get
back on duty, huh, Natsumi?

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:43.250
What's the big hurry,
all of a sudden?

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:46.760
Yeah, I've just made coffee.
Sit down and relax.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.630
Don't mind if I do! Hey! Wait!

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.730
Thanks, but we've really got to run!

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:52.100
Miyuki! Wait! Let me go!

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:55.630
Wait, Miyuki! Shoot.
She got away.

00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:03.470
Those two are a riot. I've never met
policewomen like them before.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:06.880
Keep your eyes off Miyuki. She's
my future daughter-in-law.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.780
Really? Tough luck for me.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:10.550
You've got nothing to worry about.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:12.250
What with all the girls you've got.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:16.020
Those are rumors... I'm not that lucky.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.990
You should know that.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:21.130
Anyway, your bike is your
girlfriend, right?

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:26.360
My bike never lies to me. And if I'm
good to her, she's good to me.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:32.100
What're you saying? You torture your
"precious girlfriend" in every race.

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:36.830
Well, no matter how much I torture
her, she's still my girlfriend.

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:38.880
When I beat a rival, I could
just lean down...

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:40.970
...and give her a
great big kiss!

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:43.120
You would, too!

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:46.750
Hmm... Hey, wait
a minute!

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:49.010
That's good! Yeah!
A rival!

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.280
Yuichi, will you
help me?

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:53.950
For the sake of my future
grandchildren?

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:55.220
Your grandchildren?

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:57.460
"Traffic Section"

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:01.030
Unbelievable! Yuichi Okazaki
is my relative.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.730
Yeah. He couldn't make it to your
dad's wedding because of a race.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.670
I envy that guy.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:11.010
He and I are both bikers, but
he lives right on the edge.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:13.240
Would you want to enter a
race, given the chance?

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:17.370
Sure. It'd be great to see
how I'd measure up.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:20.110
Well, if you ever get the chance, I would
be glad to work on your bike for you.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:24.420
Huh?! Then I would
win for sure!

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:30.690
By the way... Did Sena, I mean
Mom, say anything to you?

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:34.300
Uh... No, not especially.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:35.330
Really?

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:36.930
Then just forget it.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.160
Miyuki!

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:39.240
Yes?

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:40.930
Yes?
You have a guest downstairs.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.010
It's a hunky boy
on a motorbike.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:50.150
Here. This is for you.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.880
Here. This is for you.
A paddock pass! For me?

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.180
It's not just to pay you back
for fixing my bike.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:57.760
I'd really like you to come
see my next race.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.050
Judging by the work you
did on my bike...

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.820
...l'd say you know a lot
about mechanics.

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:03.590
I think you might find
it interesting.

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:06.630
Wow! Thank you.
I'd love to come!

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.160
That's good.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.400
Ooh, looks like they're
really hitting it off.

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:14.940
That's not fair. I was there
to help him, too!

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:19.040
Yeah, but when it comes to making a good
impression, Miyuki leaves you in the dust.

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:20.510
Yoriko! How can you say that?!

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:21.910
Hey, look!

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:25.850
You are all welcome
to come along, too!

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:28.020
Oops. He saw us.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:29.220
Hi there!

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:33.850
I don't believe you guys.
And you, Nakajima...

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.460
Oh, so you're him. Thank you
for taking care of Sena.

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:40.190
Not at all, if anything it's
the other way 'round.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:43.960
She tells me that you're
a great rider.

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:47.870
Well, I guess if you ride
every day like I do...

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.540
But I wonder how you'd
do in a race.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:53.110
You don't do much passing
on a police bike.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.180
Huh?

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:59.120
Huh?
I can beat anyone on a bike, race or not.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:07.460
Hmm... I wonder if he has
a thing for Miyuki.

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:08.560
Wha?!

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:10.530
There's something going on here.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:24.770
Hi, Yuichi. How
did it go?

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:27.710
It was just like
a commercial.

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:29.080
A perfect performance.

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:32.650
Good. Everything's
going as planned.

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:34.390
But I don't know about this...

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:35.450
What do you mean?

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:38.180
Nakajima didn't look too happy
about the whole thing.

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:43.330
Well, if we don't do this, those
two will never get it going.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:46.870
But if he has a rival, he won't be able
to sit on his hands anymore. Right?

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:50.000
A rival, huh?

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.210
Whoa!

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:03.340
Okazaki of Cosmo Racing
has just pulled ahead...

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:05.510
...blocking those
behind him...

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:08.490
...with his impeccable cornering
as he enters the first turn.

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:16.060
They're into the home-
stretch now!

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:18.720
They're in the final lap
and Okazaki leads!

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:20.990
Go for it!

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:22.190
Hey, watch it!

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:27.700
Go, Yuichi!

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:30.740
What do you think of my cousin?
Pretty great, huh?

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:31.880
Well, Ken?

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:35.180
He really has a feel for it. That's so much
more impressive than mere technique.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:39.310
If he has a good mechanic
too, well then... Hmm?

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:47.120
Okazaki is in the lead... The
checkered flag is out...

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:52.490
Ladies and gentlemen, Okazaki
has won the race!

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.400
Yippee! He won!

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:56.400
Okazaki, you're
wonderful!

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:07.310
Congratulations, Yuichi!

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:08.580
Thanks, Sena!

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:11.150
I'll put this one down to the
support of beautiful ladies.

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:12.840
Unreal race!

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:14.680
I feel like I won,
or something!

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:17.410
How can you
go so fast?!

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:19.420
I take short cuts.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:20.590
But it's a secret.

00:11:20.590 --> 00:11:22.560
But it's a secret.
Come off it!

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.420
You like my bike?

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:29.300
Oh, sorry. I was just...

00:11:29.470 --> 00:11:32.200
Why don't you go take
a closer look?

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:33.640
Really?!

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:35.230
Really?!
Sure, go ahead.

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:38.340
Wow! It's so
different!

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:41.110
What do you think?

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:42.380
What do you think?
It's unreal!

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:45.080
Every single part is
premium stock.

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:48.280
This bike is a work of art. It's
made with such precision.

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:50.150
That's amazing!

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:51.750
You can tell all that just
by looking at it?

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:53.880
What do you think
of that?

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.900
Isn't that a...

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:56.030
Yeah, that's right.

00:11:56.030 --> 00:11:57.460
Isn't that a...
Don't you mind, Ken?

00:11:57.460 --> 00:11:58.660
Mind what?
Don't you mind, Ken?

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:03.530
Yuichi's going to steal Miyuki away
from you if you're not careful.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.860
Steal her? She's not
an object, you know.

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:09.970
Women can fall for that kind
of charm, don't you know?

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:11.640
What are you talking about?

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:16.970
Let down your guard before the finish line,
and someone might cut you off and win.

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:20.910
Uh, I think I'll go check
out that bike, too.

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:24.490
Yes! That's the spirit!

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:27.450
You can't tell from
the outside...

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:30.220
...but the compression ratio in
the combustion chamber...

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:34.270
...has been set higher for more
power and better response.

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:36.300
Really? Oh, Nakajima!

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:37.270
Really? Oh, Nakajima!
Hi.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.870
Nakajima, you know we
could probably...

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:43.530
...make your ZXR a little more
powerful. Want to try?

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:45.130
Hmm? Well...

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:47.910
No. I wouldn't
push it.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:51.920
It'd be too hard to handle for
an ordinary rider, that is.

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:53.780
He'd be able
to handle it.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.650
He can ride
any bike.

00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:58.590
Uh, well...

00:12:58.760 --> 00:12:59.380
Really?

00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:03.520
Your bike seems to have a
real narrow power band...

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:08.530
...and I noticed a nasty imbalance
as you took that last corner.

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:15.340
But you're a real pro. I'm impressed
that you held on and won.

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:17.930
You don't miss a
thing, do you?

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:20.340
I see. So that's why
Miyuki trusts you.

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:24.040
If knowledge is all you
needed to win...

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:28.010
...then they wouldn't
need racers like me.

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:30.060
Miyuki!

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:31.250
Yes?

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:34.820
Will you come to see
me race again?

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:37.660
There's nothing that
I'd like more...

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:39.320
...but it all depends on
if it's my day off.

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:43.330
How about quitting your job and
becoming my mechanic?

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:45.100
What?!

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:47.740
Miyuki, I like you.

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:53.570
There are many skilled mechanics, but
few understand racers like me.

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:56.510
You're different. I feel that I can
place my life in your hands.

00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:58.240
Oh, my.

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:01.320
Just as you tune a bike
for someone special...

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.620
...I want to race for
someone special.

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:07.590
I'm very flattered, but...

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:09.380
She can't!

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:12.800
Why's that?

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:15.090
Because she's... uh...

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:17.070
Come on! You can do it!

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:20.570
I mean...

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:24.340
If this were a race, one moment of
hesitation could cost your life.

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.350
This isn't a race.

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:28.280
This isn't a race.
No. It's the same.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:29.680
Oh, come on!

00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:31.610
He's got to just spit
it right out!

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:35.310
If he could do that, they'd have
been an item ages ago.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.520
Nakajima.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:42.160
How about having a
race against me?

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:43.620
A race?

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:46.130
A week from today.

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:50.290
The prize is this great mechanic
here. How about it?

00:14:52.010 --> 00:14:55.070
I'll lend you my T-bike.

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:56.810
Then you won't need a handicap.

00:14:56.810 --> 00:15:00.540
Then you won't need a handicap.
Hang on! We can't bet on Kobayakawa.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:02.250
Go for it, Nakajima!

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.440
Tsujimoto!

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:05.580
Don't worry about the stakes. You
just have to win, that's all.

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:06.790
Natsumi!

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:08.120
It's not that simple!

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:12.380
You'll never get another chance
to race with a pro like him!

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:14.760
So quit all this talking and
just get it over with.

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:16.330
You'll feel better
if you do.

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:20.360
So it's settled.

00:15:20.470 --> 00:15:23.400
I'm definitely not going to
back out of this one.

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:25.330
All right, Nakajima?

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:30.310
All right.

00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:30.970
Excellent!

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:34.180
What?!

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:35.150
Huh?

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:38.550
Wait a sec, Yuichi, this isn't
what we discussed!

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:41.920
I'm sorry, Sena, but I've
changed my mind.

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:44.790
I really want Miyuki
for myself.

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:48.160
I don't care if Nakajima
is a relative...

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:50.130
...if he won't grab her, I will.

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:52.560
...if he won't grab her, I will.
You can't do that! Hello?

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:57.170
Huh?

00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:01.970
What'll I do?

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:08.210
So you're the one who put
Yuichi up to this, Sena?

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:10.980
I thought it was all happening
a little too fast.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:15.240
All I was trying to do was get
Ken and Miyuki together.

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:19.820
I've been hoping something would
happen between them, too.

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:24.850
I never would have guessed that
Yuichi would fall for her.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.690
If Ken loses...

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:28.960
...Yuichi's going to take
her for himself.

00:16:29.140 --> 00:16:30.900
IF he loses, right?

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:35.000
It seems like the Goddess of Com-
petition has chosen the winner.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.630
Huh?

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:51.890
Hmm. Maybe it's too tight. No...

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:52.950
Nakajima!

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:55.750
Well? How's
it going?

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:58.560
Oh, all right,
I guess.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:16:59.630
Oh, wait...

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:02.330
That's okay. I'll do it myself.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:06.270
Wouldn't be fair if you
helped me, would it?

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.500
No, I guess not.

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:11.940
Umm, listen...

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:14.110
What is it?

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:17.210
What is it?
I just feel kind of bad...

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:21.250
...having this bet be
about you, and all.

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:24.660
But honestly, I'm
very pleased.

00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:27.590
I'm going to be able to
race Yuichi Okazaki.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:30.530
This bet thing isn't the best
reason for racing him...

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:34.330
...but I'll put that out of my mind,
and just do my best.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:37.090
...And you... uh, you... well,
no matter what the result...

00:17:37.270 --> 00:17:41.000
...it's... uh... well, I'd
want to properly...

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:44.380
...well... at the
right time...

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:49.210
Aah... I'm no good
at this!

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:10.600
Hmm... Sounds good.

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:12.470
Looks like you've done a good job!

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:16.110
Well, I think I've fixed it up all right.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:18.010
"All right?" That's not good enough!

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:20.850
Ken, you just
have to win!

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:23.140
You can't lose! If you
do, it'll be tragic!

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:24.480
You understand that, don't you?

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:26.210
Huh?!

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:35.050
Good morning.

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:37.490
I'm glad you came,
Miyuki.

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:40.890
I'm ready to go
when you are.

00:18:46.510 --> 00:18:49.480
I can give you a head
start, if you like.

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:51.430
No thanks, I don't
need it.

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:52.980
Let's have a
good race!

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:54.880
Of course.

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:10.490
Are you ready?

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:12.520
Get set!

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:14.060
Go!

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:18.790
Feel that tension.

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:21.800
Come on, Ken!

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:37.580
Look at him! He's
doing all right.

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:39.280
Come on. You
can do it!

00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:47.100
<i>He's still on my tail.</i>

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:56.030
This is going to
be a close one.

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:00.010
Nakajima...

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:10.760
Here they come!

00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:11.850
Who's ahead?!

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:36.380
Congratulations,
you beat me.

00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:38.180
Come on.

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:41.340
We came in practically at the same
time. You can't tell who was first.

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:45.520
I've been in a lot of races, but I just
couldn't get it together this time.

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:51.660
My mind was wandering all over the place,
and I lost. You were totally focused.

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:54.960
I sort of drowned out
everything else.

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:57.830
That's the most important
thing in a race.

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:02.810
But lately something's happened to me.
I guess I've had a lot on my mind.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:07.180
I've forgotten the most important
thing about racing... having fun.

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:11.370
But if you keep dawdling,
I'll be back for Miyuki.

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:14.380
Yeah. Gotcha.

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:18.850
Sena! Looks like you're going to
get your grandchildren after all.

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:22.590
Yuichi! You don't have
to tell everybody!

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:26.390
Sena's grandchildren, huh? Now
who's children would that be?

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:27.690
Natsumi!

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:29.730
Come off it,
Yuichi!

00:21:29.900 --> 00:21:33.100
Like I said, you have to
have fun in a race.

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:37.630
You still haven't crossed the finish
line with Miyuki, you know?

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:39.470
You mustn't be
complacent.

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:41.010
Yeah, I guess
you're right.

00:21:55.290 --> 00:22:00.800
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:11.410
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:18.310
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:28.430
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:42.440
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:42.740 --> 00:22:50.570
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:59.260
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:22:59.490 --> 00:23:06.470
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:10.470 --> 00:23:16.870
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.280 --> 00:23:24.350
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:26.450 --> 00:23:27.780
"Time is running out..."

00:23:28.250 --> 00:23:30.420
It's my day off! I'm
goin' shoppin'!

00:23:30.590 --> 00:23:33.620
Titanium alloy, a professional screw-
driver, mountain climbing rope...

00:23:33.730 --> 00:23:35.190
...a tea kettle, ladle
and a pot...

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:36.290
Whatcha need them for?

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:38.760
It's a bomb! Somebody put a bomb
inside a department store!

00:23:38.930 --> 00:23:40.230
You're using that junk
to disarm the bomb?

00:23:40.230 --> 00:23:41.170
Time is running out!

00:23:41.170 --> 00:23:44.030
And look how we're dressed!
Time is running out!

00:23:44.200 --> 00:23:46.330
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 30...

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:46.470
..."Forever My Beloved Riko."

00:23:46.470 --> 00:23:48.140
FILE. 30
FOREVER MY
BELOVED RIKO

00:23:48.140 --> 00:23:51.310
I've blown my
day off!
